ADS-003 — Canonical Atlas Object (CAO)

Document ID: ADS-003
Title: Canonical Atlas Object (CAO)
Version: 1.0.0-draft
Status: Draft

1. Purpose

This specification defines the Canonical Atlas Object (CAO), the foundational object model for all governed entities within the Atlas Engineering Cognition Framework (AECF).

Every governed Atlas entity SHALL be represented as a Canonical Atlas Object or a specialization thereof.

The CAO provides a unified contract for identity, metadata, governance, lifecycle, provenance, security, traceability, and extensibility.

2. Scope

This specification defines:

Canonical object model
Object inheritance
Mandatory properties
Identity model
Metadata model
Governance model
Lifecycle model
Extension model

This specification applies to every governed Atlas object.

3. Canonical Definition

A Canonical Atlas Object (CAO) is the universal, technology-independent representation of a governed Atlas entity, providing a common semantic, governance, lifecycle, and interoperability contract inherited by all Atlas object types.

4. Objectives

The CAO SHALL:

Provide a universal root object.
Standardize governance.
Standardize metadata.
Standardize lifecycle.
Standardize versioning.
Standardize security.
Standardize traceability.
Enable extensibility.
5. CAO Axiom

The following statement is normative.

Every governed Atlas entity SHALL be represented as exactly one Canonical Atlas Object (CAO) or a specialization thereof.

No governed entity SHALL bypass the CAO.

