7. Mandatory Properties

Every CAO SHALL include the following mandatory properties.

Property	Description
Object ID	Globally unique identifier
Object Type	Canonical Atlas type
Object Name	Human-readable name
Version	Object version
Schema Version	Governing schema version
Lifecycle State	Current lifecycle state
Status	Operational status
Created Timestamp	Creation time
Modified Timestamp	Last modification time
Owner	Responsible authority
Steward	Governance steward
Security Classification	Data classification
Metadata	Canonical metadata
Provenance	Origin information
Traceability	Relationships to other objects

These properties SHALL exist for every CAO.

8. Identity Model

Each CAO SHALL possess:

Immutable Object ID
Persistent identity
Globally unique identifier
Type identifier
Namespace
Version identity

Identity SHALL remain stable throughout the object lifecycle.

9. Metadata Model

Every CAO SHALL expose metadata including:

Title
Description
Keywords
Domain
Discipline
Language
Tags
Creator
Organization
Created Date
Last Modified
Documentation References

Metadata SHALL support discovery and interoperability.

10. Governance Model

Every CAO SHALL define:

Owner
Steward
Custodian
Approval Authority
Retention Policy
Validation Policy
Access Policy
Audit Requirements

Governance SHALL remain attached to the object throughout its lifecycle.

11. Provenance Model

Every CAO SHALL preserve:

Origin
Producer
Source artifacts
Transformations
Parent objects
Derived objects
Processing history

Provenance SHALL be immutable.

12. Traceability Model

Every CAO SHALL support explicit relationships.

Supported relationship types include:

derivesFrom
references
dependsOn
validates
supersedes
generates
consumedBy
approvedBy
relatedTo

Relationships SHALL be directional and typed.

13. Lifecycle Model

Every CAO SHALL support:

Draft
   │
Validated
   │
Approved
   │
Active
   │
Superseded
   │
Archived
   │
Retired

Lifecycle transitions SHALL preserve historical records.

14. Extension Model

Atlas objects MAY introduce additional properties.

Extensions SHALL:

Preserve canonical semantics.
Maintain backward compatibility.
Avoid redefining inherited properties.
Remain version-aware.

Specializations SHALL inherit all mandatory CAO properties.

15. Quality Requirements

Every CAO SHALL satisfy:

Accuracy
Completeness
Consistency
Validity
Integrity
Traceability
Explainability
Governance compliance

Quality SHALL be measurable.

16. Conformance

A Canonical Atlas Object conforms if it:

Implements all mandatory properties.
Preserves immutable identity.
Maintains governance information.
Preserves provenance.
Implements lifecycle management.
Supports typed relationships.
Supports version management.
17. Future Evolution

Future revisions MAY introduce:

Ontology bindings.
Semantic web compatibility.
Knowledge graph integration.
Digital engineering extensions.
Domain-specific profiles.

Such extensions SHALL remain compatible with the CAO contract.

